.TH setjmp.h 3 scc\-VERSION
.SH NAME
setjmp.h - support for non-local jumps
.SH SYNOPSIS

#include <setjmp.h>

The setjmp.h header declares the following functions:

.nf
void longjmp(jmp_buf env, int val)
int setjmp(jmp_buf env)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The setjmp.h header defines the type

.B jmp_buf

This is an array type large enough to hold all information
required to restore the execution state of a call to
.BR setjmp ,
so that
.B longjmp
can later return execution to that point as if the block were
being re-entered.
.SH STANDARDS
ISO/IEC 9899:1999 Section 7.13.1 Paragraph 1,2,3
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setjmp (3)
.BR longjmp (3)
